<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">House of Grimaldi</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The House of Grimaldi is a family of Genoese origin that has ruled Monaco since 1297, when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francois-grimaldi">François Grimaldi</a> seized its fortress. One of the great Guelph clans of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/genoa">Genoa</a>, the family lost and regained Monaco several times before securing it in the 15th century, and from 1612 its rulers styled themselves princes. The present line descends from Princess Louise-Hippolyte, whose husband took the Grimaldi name in 1731.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/house-of-grimaldi.jpg" alt="House of Grimaldi" width="320" height="330" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Great_coat_of_arms_of_the_house_of_Grimaldi.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
